  "preamble": "Dissibilation of the voiced dental/alveolar affricate [dz] to the voiced non-sibilant dental fricative [ð]: the stop closure is lost and the sibilant groove flattens. In Albanian, the Early Proto-Albanian reflex *dz of the Proto-Indo-European palatovelars *ǵ and *ǵʰ became dh /ð/ (dhëmb 'tooth', i madh 'big', rrjedh 'flow').",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deaffrication, Dissibilation, Interdentalization",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Proto-Albanian to Albanian",
      "languageFamily": "Albanian",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Early Proto-Albanian *dzamba (< PIE *ǵómbʰos)",
          "to": "dhëmb [ðəmb] 'tooth' (Gheg dhamb)",
          "note": "The palatal series *ǵ, *ǵʰ gives *dz > *ð, written dh, parallel to *ḱ > *ts > *θ > th (EPA *tserā > thjerë 'lentil')."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Albanian *màdza (< PIE *méǵh₂os)",
          "to": "i madh 'big'"
        },
        {
          "from": "Early Proto-Albanian *redza (< PIE *h₃reǵ-)",
          "to": "rrjedh 'to flow'"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
